      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/reader_west_virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Benjamin Reader once purchased six hundred acres of land for just a ten-gallon copper kettle and a bay mare.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/reader_west_virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The community of Reader got its start around 1901 when the railroad was extended to that point.",
